The clone has a modified file, but the program does not report it and exits with status 0, because
the version control program does not exist.  The program reports unpushed commits, because it could
not tell that there are none.  The goal files record the current (wrong) behavior: a user who
misspells --git-executable is not told so.  The program does try to report this, but the report is
unreachable, because commons-exec passes the failure to the result handler instead of throwing
IOException from the asynchronous execute method.
